From: mica <mica@localhost>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] s7d: preserve the installer receipt across defenv

The complete eMMC burn recreates the redundant environment and saves the
installer receipt, but the replacement bootloader's first boot then runs the
vendor default-environment migration.  The common reserve list does not own
the BM201-specific receipt, so that migration drops it before the installer
gate runs and the same package is installed again.

Keep the vendor migration and select the board-local reserve list alongside
the common list.  Reserve only the BM201 receipt in that list.  This leaves
the shared Amlogic reserve policy and upgrade_step transition unchanged.

---
diff --git a/bl33/v2023/board/amlogic/s7d_bm201/s7d_bm201.c b/bl33/v2023/board/amlogic/s7d_bm201/s7d_bm201.c
index 8668fd8c..9569ea0d 100644
--- a/bl33/v2023/board/amlogic/s7d_bm201/s7d_bm201.c
+++ b/bl33/v2023/board/amlogic/s7d_bm201/s7d_bm201.c
@@ -48,11 +48,17 @@
 #endif
 #include <amlogic/aml_profile.h>
 
+#include "bm201_emmc_installer.h"
 #include "boot_source_logic.h"
 
 DECLARE_GLOBAL_DATA_PTR;
 extern int cc_statue, bc_status;
 
+const char * const _board_env_reserv_array0[] = {
+	BM201_INSTALLER_RECEIPT_ENV,
+	NULL
+};
+
 void sys_led_init(void)
 {
 }
@@ -318,9 +324,9 @@ int board_late_init(void)
 	int ret;
 
 	printf("board late init\n");
-	env_set("defenv_para", "-c");
+	env_set("defenv_para", "-c -b0");
 	if (env_get_ulong("default_env", 10, 0))
-		env_set("defenv_para", "-c0"); //andr factory reset or factory burn
+		env_set("defenv_para", "-c0 -b0"); //andr factory reset or factory burn
 	aml_board_late_init_front(NULL);
 #ifdef CONFIG_PXP_EMULATOR
 	return 0;
